From 29d516e932c5362f271e3cf22a23be700f097e4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:45:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: fork to a sub-thread from any turn's controls
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.33 (ask 55). Story 039's fork (0070) is offered
from a selection's context menu and copies the whole conversation. The
operator asked for a fork icon on each turn, after its stats, that keeps
the conversation only up to that turn.

- acp_thread: AssistantMessage::last_message_id reads the ACP id the
  agent stamped on its reply chunks, which the thread already keeps in
  each chunk's MessageIdentity; nothing new is stored. AgentConnection
  gains supports_fork_at_turn and fork_session_at(.., cut), refusing by
  default: forking the whole conversation instead would silently keep
  the turns the user asked to leave out.
- agent_servers (v1): fork_session's body becomes fork_session_with(..,
  cut); with a cut, the `session/fork` request carries
  `_meta["_claude/forkAt"]`, which Claude Agent (Plus) 0.38.0 resolves to
  its transcript. The cut is offered when the agent advertises
  session/fork and `_claude/rewind` -- plus ships both in 0.38.0, so that
  capability is the signal.
- agent_ui: the controls row under every finished turn (render_thread_
  controls, which now knows its entry) gains a GitBranchPlus button,
  "Fork to a Sub-thread from Here", on the root session's view, disabled
  while a turn runs, as 0070's menu entry is. sub_thread::turn_fork::
  turn_cut names the turn by its last agent message id ({"messageId"}),
  or by its 1-based position among the prompts ({"turn"}) when no reply
  carries one; the id is never taken from an earlier turn.
  AgentPanel::open_sub_thread_at opens 0070's "with context" sub-thread
  through fork_session_at; the inherited count covers the kept turns.
  The click defers the opening past the view's update: the first build
  panicked there ("already being updated"), found by the Xvfb proof.

Tests: turn_fork::tests (the last reply id names the turn; an earlier
turn's id is never used; nothing before the first prompt) -- seen
failing with the search allowed past the turn's user message -- and
fork_session_tests::a_cut_point_goes_under_the_fork_at_meta_key_only_
when_given. The sub-thread suites and acp_thread pass. Xvfb proof with a
stub agent: docs/assets/zeo-6.33-fork-from-turn-2026-11-15/ in the hub
(the stub received {"_claude/forkAt": {"messageId": "msg_1"}} and the
sub-thread inherited the first turn's two messages).
---

